    <p>Three things set your price:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Site size and technical debt.</strong> A 20-page brochure site needs less work than a 5,000-product catalogue. Bigger sites mean more crawl management, internal linking, and content governance.</li>
      <li><strong>Keyword competition.</strong> "Plumber Solihull" is easier than "business insurance Birmingham." Harder keywords demand more content, stronger links, and longer timelines.</li>
      <li><strong>Industry regulation.</strong> Finance, health, and legal sites need demonstrable expertise, authoritative backlinks, and professionally reviewed content. That costs more than a standard service page.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We explain exactly which factors apply to you and why the number is what it is. If an agency cannot justify its quote with specifics, walk away.</p>

