      <li><strong>Direct access.</strong> You talk to the person doing the work. No account manager buffer. Email, phone, video. Response in hours, not days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>ROI: What Birmingham Businesses Can Expect</h2>

    <p>SEO is an investment. Here is what the return curve looks like across Birmingham businesses we have worked with:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Months 1-3:</strong> Technical fixes. Crawl errors gone. Site speed up. Google Business Profile optimised. This alone drives 10-20% more impressions.</li>
      <li><strong>Months 3-6:</strong> Content strategy lands. New pages rank. Old pages climb. Expect 30-60% organic traffic growth from baseline if you had zero prior SEO.</li>
      <li><strong>Months 6-12:</strong> Compounding hits. Links build authority. Competitive keywords reach page one. Organic traffic doubles. Leads follow.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>The metric that matters is revenue per pound spent. A <a href="/services/">well-run SEO campaign</a> returns £3-£8 for every £1 within 12 months. Returns accelerate as domain authority compounds.</p>

    <h2>Industries and Typical Budgets in Birmingham</h2>

    <p>Birmingham is diverse. SEO budgets reflect that. Here is what different sectors typically invest.</p>

    <h3>Jewellery Quarter Retailers</h3>

    <p>Independent jewellers in the <strong>Jewellery Quarter</strong> invest £497-£997 per month. Competition is moderate for product terms like "bespoke diamond ring Birmingham." Margins are high enough that one organic lead pays for three months of SEO. Visual content, product schema, and Google Shopping integration drive the work.</p>

    <h3>Colmore Business District Professional Services</h3>

    <p>Law firms and accountants on <strong>Colmore Row</strong> face the fiercest SEO competition in Birmingham. £997-£1,997 per month is standard. One commercial property instruction or corporate retainer pays for a full year of fees. Content must prove genuine expertise to satisfy Google's E-E-A-T requirements for legal and financial topics.</p>

    <h3>Digbeth Startups and Creative Agencies</h3>

